source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Show the decisions behind the site, or behind one file.

Usage: ink explain [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Examples
  # Why one file looks the way it does
  ink explain posts/a.md

  # Replay one decision, rung by rung
  ink explain posts/a.md --why page.title

Arguments
  [PATH]  A file of the folder, as a path in it: only its
          decisions. Without one, every decision

Options
      --why <CODE>  Replay one decision's ladder, rung by
                    rung: `ink explain posts/a.md --why
                    page.title`, or a site code alone
                    (`--why site.title`)

Source
      --source <KIND>  `folder` reads the files on disk,
                       `git` reads a commit [default: `git`
                       when .git exists, said as a notice]
      --rev <REV>      The commit to read, as `git
                       rev-parse` takes it; only for a git
                       repository [default: HEAD]

Exit codes
  0  Done; warnings, if any, were printed
  1  The site has errors
  2  Wrong usage, or a folder that is missing; nothing was
     changed

See also  ink pin, ink select
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log,
          --log-file (see `ink --help`)
